  // The main tabs
  'HOME: the first tab. It has the NGMY brand, the Helper AI, loans, and the tech frames: Neural Link, Signal Grid, Core Protocol and the Vault Channel arcade.',
  'SIGNAL GRID FOR MEMBERS AND SIGNAL ALERTS: admins tapping Signal Grid get the paper trading agent; every other member gets the Trading Academy (lessons, live signals and the tutor). Each lesson has a 10 question quiz drawn from 14 questions, with the answers in a new order each time. For members a wrong answer gets one more try; wrong twice and that question locks for 5 minutes, then a different question with different answers takes its place (admins can always retry). All 10 questions right finishes the lesson, and progress is saved on the server. Finishing all 10 lessons unlocks signal alerts; admins always have them. A signal alert says ENTER UP (buy or call) or ENTER DOWN (sell or put), the market name, enter within so many minutes and the duration in minutes, and only comes for signals that are clear, still early and worked at least half the time lately on that market. Alerts come only for the market the agent trades today (SPY on weekdays while the stock market is open, BTC/USD on weekends), never for forex or other markets, and never an ENTER UP into a falling big trend. Every Live signal (the agent markets and all forex pairs) follows the same big trend rule as the agent: ENTER UP only when the slow average is higher than 1 hour ago and the price is above it, and ENTER DOWN only when the slow average is lower than 1 hour ago and the price is below it. Otherwise the card says UP BUT BIG TREND FALLING, SKIP or DOWN BUT BIG TREND RISING, SKIP. Alerts work like the other NGMY notifications: while the app is open or in the background, after allowing notifications. Every market has ONE decision, the same on the label, the big sign, the frame, the counts and the alerts: ENTER UP (buy) or ENTER DOWN (sell), UP or DOWN BUT TOO LATE (wait), UP or DOWN BUT WEAK (skip, because that move failed too often on this market lately), NO CLEAR DIRECTION (wait), or MARKET CLOSED. When it is ENTER, a big sign at the top of the card shows the direction, a live countdown in seconds to the start of the next candle (Enter in 0:36, then ENTER NOW at zero), and how long to trade for in minutes. The DECISION AND DURATION frame at the bottom repeats the decision in one plain sentence and the facts it is based on. The counts at the top are Going up, Going down and No direction. On the Signal Grid agent screen the paper balance moves with every pretend win and loss (plus the open pretend trade), on top of the Alpaca paper account, which itself stays the same because Version 1 sends no orders.',
